## The Cushion Divide

Not all cushion cuts are the same. This is the single most important fact any cushion cut buyer needs to know before purchasing.

Two variants exist: **cushion modified brilliant** and **cushion brilliant**. The certificate will say which one you have. Most cushion cuts on the market are cushion modified.

The cushion modified brilliant has an extra row of small facets under the girdle. This creates a sparkle pattern sometimes called "crushed ice" — a fine, scattered glitter effect rather than chunky flashes.

Some buyers love it. Others find it too busy.

The cushion brilliant omits those extra girdle facets. The result is larger, more defined light flashes. The sparkle pattern reads as more like a round brilliant — bigger individual flashes rather than a sea of micro-scintillation.

This is The Cushion Divide: two diamonds with the same shape name, the same certificate category, but meaningfully different light performance. Neither is better — they are different aesthetics.

But you cannot tell which variant you have from a photo. You must watch a video of the specific stone.

**Why this matters vs. the emerald cut:**

The emerald cut has no equivalent ambiguity. All emerald cuts are step cuts. The light performance you see in one emerald cut is the same fundamental character you will see in every emerald cut.

The only variables are how well the stone is cut and how clean the clarity and color are.

Cushion cut buyers must know which variant they are buying. Emerald cut buyers have no such complication. This is one practical advantage of the emerald cut that rarely gets mentioned.

**Quick reference — cushion modified vs cushion brilliant:**

<table class="dc-custom-table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Characteristic</th>
