## Clarity: What Each Shape Hides and Shows

The clarity difference is the most important practical factor separating these two shapes.

**Cushion cut clarity floor: VS2 (GIA)**

The cushion's brilliant facets scatter incoming light. Inclusions are fragmented across the scintillation pattern and become invisible to the naked eye. GIA VS2 is almost always eye-clean in a cushion.

SI1 can be eye-clean if the inclusion is near the girdle — always watch a video to confirm.

**Emerald cut clarity floor: VS1 (GIA)**

The step-cut's open table has no scattered light to hide inclusions. A feather or crystal at the center of the table is visible at arm's length. VS2 in an emerald cut is risky without first checking the clarity plot.

VS1 is the safe floor for an eye-clean result.

SI1 in an emerald cut almost always shows. It is not recommended.

