## Color: How Each Shape Reads in Different Metals

**Cushion cut color floor: H (GIA) in white gold**

The cushion's brilliant facets break body color into sparkle. H-color reads white to most eyes in platinum or white gold. Buyers who set the cushion in yellow gold can often go as warm as I or J — the warm metal absorbs the warmth in the stone.

**Emerald cut color floor: G (GIA) in white gold**

The step-cut's long unbroken reflections show body color as a warmth in the light. H-color in an emerald cut set in platinum reads slightly warm to trained eyes. G is the safe minimum for a color-neutral appearance.

