## Proportions: What to Target for Each Shape

**Cushion cut proportions:**
- Length-to-width ratio: 1.00–1.10 for a square cushion. 1.10–1.25 for a slightly elongated look. Above 1.30 starts to look like a short emerald cut.
- Depth: 60–67% is the accepted range. Very deep cushions (above 68%) look small face-up for their weight.
- Table: 58–68% is the preferred range.
- Polish and Symmetry: Very Good or Excellent minimum.
- Critical check: whether you are buying cushion modified or cushion brilliant. Check the certificate.

**Emerald cut proportions:**
- Length-to-width ratio: 1.30–1.50 for the classic elongated look. Below 1.30 looks nearly square (close to Asscher territory). Above 1.55 looks dramatically narrow.
- Depth: 60–64% ideal. Shallower stones (below 58%) window — light passes through without reflecting.
- Table: 61–69% preferred.
- Polish and Symmetry: Excellent or Very Good. The large flat facets amplify any asymmetry.

