## Face-Up Size: Which Shape Looks Bigger?

Both shapes look larger than a round brilliant at the same carat weight. The mechanism is the same: weight is distributed shallower and wider rather than deep.

A 2ct round brilliant measures approximately 8.1mm in diameter. A 2ct square cushion measures approximately 7.5×7.5mm — only slightly smaller than the round, but the rounded corners give it a softer, more organic silhouette on the finger. A 2ct emerald cut measures approximately 8.5×6mm — narrower in width but longer, creating a rectangular footprint that reads differently across the finger.

On the finger, the emerald cut often appears longer. The cushion appears more compact and pillowy. Neither is objectively larger — they have similar total face-up areas, but the shape of that area differs completely.

**Approximate face-up dimensions by carat:**

